      """
      {"openai_models": "", "debug": "true"}
      """
    When the action runs
    Then chat request 1 used model "gpt-5.3-codex" temperature 1.0 and max tokens 3072
    And a log line containing "Using options:" was recorded

  Scenario: errors are swallowed without debug
    Given the action context has no pull request payload
    And no PR comments are routed
    When the action runs
    Then it resolves to undefined
    And a log line containing "fake github: unexpected graphql" was recorded
    And no labels were added

  Scenario: errors are rethrown with debug
    Given the environment variable DEBUG is "true"
    And the action context has no pull request payload
    And no PR comments are routed
    When the action runs
    Then it rejects with an error containing "fake github: unexpected graphql"

  Scenario: config, properties and inputs override in precedence order
    Given a config file ".github/pull-merge.json" containing:
      """
      {"amplification": "5"}
      """
    And repo properties:
      | property_name | value |
      | pull_merge_amplification | 3 |
      | pull_merge_max_tokens | 512 |
    And the action inputs:
      """
      {"max_tokens": "256", "include_diff": "true", "debug": "true"}
      """
    When the action runs
    Then chat request 1 used model "gpt-5.3-codex" temperature 1.0 and max tokens 256
    And a log line containing '"amplification":3' was recorded
    And a comment was created containing "<details><summary>Diff</summary>"
    And the puLL-Merge label was added

